Reading: uniform fractional parts would be 0.2500. Every stack is
below that, so some locking is always present; what varies is how
much, and it varies with the scene exactly as rule 6 says shrinkage
does. n=6 with one pair each is thin, and the two rank inversions
are between stacks whose shrinkage differs little (3.26 vs 2.20,
1.32 vs 1.05). This is offered as a candidate mechanism for a
relationship rule 6 currently records as unpredictable, not as a
settled law.
